{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status","id":1005271,"title":"Metis Social Status VS Kinfolk Social Status","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-19T00:48:45-08:00","id":1005271,"title":"Metis Social Status VS Kinfolk Social Status","content":"One very blurry issue that has not really been properly addressed across the books.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk are second class citizens 99% of the time in Garou Society no matter how accomplished/educated they are in Human Society.<br /> <br /> Heck, even Bone Gnawer Kinfolk who can hold jobs and have Level-3 Resources have to drop EVERYTHING for their illiterate, never-even-ONE-Dot Resource Garou Crackhead-cousins if they drop by on Saturday Night riddled with bullets, and have to just nod their heads and smile while missing out on Junior's Piano Recital.<br /> <br /> And yet they are afforded respect, honor and love because they provide the vital role of being able to give birth to/sire the children of the next generation of Garou.<br /> <br /> Whereas Metis are CONSISTENTLY described as whipping boys and objects of mockery not just for their physical and/or mental deformities, but for the fact that they bring NOTHING reproductively to the table: They are literally just eating up oxygen and food, waiting to die while not being able to give the Garou more children for the future.<br /> <br /> So: My Question Being.<br /> <br /> In terms of Social Status, a Kinfolk, particularly a financially stable, politically connected and educated one, would surely have a higher spot on the social totem pole than a Metis-Liability, right?<br /> <br /> I would imagine that ESPECIALLY in the Fianna, that disgusting tribe of whore-mongering child-abusing/abandoning hypocrites, even the KINFOLK get to bully the Metis Children and expect nothing but grateful nods from their designated tribal punching-bag?<br /> <br /> Curioser and Curioser....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-19-2016, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T02:40:36-08:00","id":1005284,"title":"","content":"Depends on the tribe, honestly. The books state that some tribes give their metis for their kinfolk to raise, since they have the time to do it. Usually this amounts to the metis being in a basement and only fed at most. For example, to Silver Fangs, kinfolk are servants so they get to deal with the lower caste.<br /> <br /> For Fianna, though, I imagine they just throw their metis into some distant part of the woods and try to forget about them.<br /> <br /> This is of course just about the child metis, adult metis are still accepted as part of a tribe. That can mean they get to be less of a punching bag to fully accepted members. And that does include watching over kinfolk at times. In fact, given their sterility, metis are perfect for being the ones handling things with kin as they are very tied to tribal ideals and sterile.<br /> <br /> For my part, I've had these situations with my metis and their kinfolk ties;<br /> <br /> - one lived in a family like a guard dog until they changed, then they were taught to be a servant and were subservient to the kinfolk.<br /> <br /> - one was sent to build a monastery with a gaggle of kinfolk monks.<br /> <br /> - one was raised by their kinfolk uncle and view them as family.<br /> <br /> - one lived with a pack of wolves and garou and acted as a guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T03:11:08-08:00","id":1005290,"title":"","content":"In terms of status, would they still be below a kin? Surely a Senator Politician Kinfolk who is key to keeping a Caern from being bulldozed and chopped up into toothpicks would have a higher status than a hunchback and mute metis who can't even go out in public, much less make a difference?<br /> <br /> On a side note, In My Honest Opinion the Fianna Tribe's treatment of Metis is despicable in the same way that teenage parents like &quot;Juno&quot; who give up their babies for adoption to finish High-School but never even LOOK at them, much less love and care about them again are despicable.<br /> <br /> &quot;Loves to Fuck, but refuses to Love The Consequences.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-19-2016, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T05:53:13-08:00","id":1005321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1005290#post1005290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of status, would they still be below a kin? Surely a Senator Politician Kinfolk who is key to keeping a Caern from being bulldozed and chopped up into toothpicks would have a higher status than a hunchback and mute metis who can't even go out in public, much less make a difference?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That hunback might be a great theurge, easily creating fetishes. Or a good fighter, keeping the Caerns safe. They can make a -massive- difference.<br /> <br /> The fact is, that metis are garou, they can fight for Gaia in the ways kinfolk can't. That is respected, if grudgingly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T07:20:41-08:00","id":1005341,"title":"","content":"Well, speaking as someone who supports abortion, I think that Juno did the best thing for the child that she decided to bear, even if it would have been more rational for her to have an abortion. A baby who is given up for adoption in America (especially a Caucasian or half-Caucasian baby) will be given to adopted parents who have proven themselves to be kind and loving people (older children who become adoptees may have worse outcomes). Metis, however, are born obviously mutated and deformed, as they are born in Crinos form.<br /> <br /> I imagine that Garou-Garou relationships are much more common than portrayed and that female Homid Garou quietly get a surgical abortion from a Human Kinfolk doctor if they suspect that they are carrying a Metis fetus. Lupus Garou, because they regenerate in homid form, probably have less options, though they could try to find a Human Kinfolk vet. In either case, they probably end up owing a Human Kinfolk a large favor for their discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:21:14-08:00","id":1005358,"title":"","content":"It's also the <i>honorable</i> thing to do.<br /> <br /> You want to finish school? You want to hang out with your friends at the mall?<br /> But you DON'T want to Love And Care for an Innocent Child?<br /> Then *Don't Fuck AT ALL* <b>until</b> you are ready to do the latter.<br /> <br /> Or do the <b>honorable</b> thing, get an abotion, and take <b>responsibility</b> by listening to the screams of your baby in your nightmares for the rest of your life; that is if you had a conscience in the first-place.<br /> <br /> Better for a child to not even born at all than to come into a loveless world.<br /> You made your bed? *Now sleep in it!*<br /> <br /> The Fianna are disgusting hypocrites who spout and broadcast the virtue of love and family, but just like Juno, refuse to take resposibility when the chips are down, and yet are too cowardly and dishonorable to get an abortion and *live with the pain and guilt* of their lust destroying an innocent life, like ANYONE sentient enough to open their legs and WILLINGLY let another sentient being in SHOULD be mature enough to do.<br /> <br /> And those hedonistic drunken degenerates have the GALL to look down on the Get of Fenris, who Love Care-For and Respect ALL their Metis AND Kinfolk, the way a REAL Warrior should for his Family. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not bad, and very egalitarian for a so-called tribe of mindless berserkers, no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-19-2016, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T08:22:47-08:00","id":1005359,"title":"","content":"metis are sullied, Kinfolk are Lesser, somewhat different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:03:14-08:00","id":1005396,"title":"","content":"There are too many other factors that go into a question like this, that trying to simplify it to &quot;who is socially higher&quot; isn't something that can be answered.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T14:30:39-08:00","id":1005480,"title":"","content":"Not gonna touch the abortion thing (these threads veer into the weirdest places).<br /> <br /> Back to the original topic: the hierarchy isn't sharply drawn, as their roles are different. Metis are generally regarded as cursed, low-ranking grunts in the war for Gaia. Kinfolk are noncombatant support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-19-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T15:40:48-08:00","id":1005498,"title":"","content":"The books have generally presented Metis as &quot;out ranking&quot; kinfolk, because the Garou promote a hierarchy where Garou &gt; Kin. Even the lowest Garou is still a Garou.<br /> <br /> Of course the informal social weight is far more complicated. Tribal attitudes, character history, etc. are all going to matter. The kin mate of one of the Sept Elders that has decades of service to the Sept with a reputation of going above and beyond in their duties while never using their mate's status as a cudgel, is going to have a social advantage over a Metis Cub that's still in training for their Initiation. In a more traditional Sept/Tribe, that means the kin is still going to be expected to do things like defer to the Metis in terms of order of eating, or seating around a table, but the Metis would learn pretty quickly (if they hadn't already) that trying to use their rank to push said kin around is just going to result in a lot of higher ranking Garou making that Metis' life hell.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, the Fenrir don't respect all Metis and Kin. They respect merit. A Metis that proves themselves is welcomed into the Tribe. It's not a universal tolerance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T18:04:13-08:00","id":1005524,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>. Would this be a feasible scenario?<br /> <br /> ************************************************** *********<br /> <br /> A Shadow Lord emissary staggers back to his Caern, broken-arm in a splint and and a black eye. He incredulously laughed that he had returned from *the* single most *lopsided* Caern he even visited in his career.<br /> <br /> *Every* warrior at the disastrous dinner party *deferred* to a Kinfolk-Nanny, whom with most improper affection they referred to as &quot;Mama.&quot;<br /> <br /> They held the door open for her, they let her speak before they did, hugged her with open affection, let her sit down at the table *before* them, and most horrifying of all, allow her gentle-suggestions to carry *Equal* weight to that of the Alpha's when it concerned the safety and emotional well being of the Caern's children.<br /> <br /> And *all* he did, scoffed the Shadow Lord, was scream &quot;You Clumsy Old Bitch!!&quot; and raised his hand to hit her when she accidentally tripped and spilled a drink in his lap.<br /> <br /> EVERY Warrior at the table, Homid Metis *and* Lupus, whom &quot;Mama&quot; had raised, played with, taught, fed, hugged, healed, comforted and loved like her own children, rose up as one in a *heartbeat* and beat the ever-loving daylights out of the Shadow Lord emissary for daring to threaten their beloved &quot;Mother.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the final &quot;indignity&quot;? Had it not being for the pleas of &quot;Mama&quot; herself, hugging the Alpha, and with firm kindness whispered &quot;it's alright&quot; until he melted from murderous Crinos back to furious Homid, followed by *her* formal and humble apology towards the Shadow Lord, he would have have been turned into sushi.<br /> <br /> *She* was even the one who made the splint for his broken arm, followed by a glass of hot milk and a smile.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh the improper impudence of it all&quot; mumbled the Shadow Lord as he munched into one of Mama's delicious home-baked chocolate chip cookies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ************************************************** ********<br /> <br /> On reflection (especially the memories of growing up in a Taiwanese/Chinese Background), the Dignity and Strength of Character built from being a Kind Grandmother, not to mention the Love her (grand)children will feel for her tends to carry a LOT of weight in *any* family, *probably* even a Garou one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-24-2016, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T19:06:53-08:00","id":1005537,"title":"","content":"Sounds pretty much exactly like the kind of faux pas a more traditional Garou might face around any of the less formal Tribes.<br /> <br /> The least reasonable part of the scenario is a Shadowlord (or really any Garou) that's trained and trusted as an emissary being stupid enough to not recognize the situation; esp. insulting an Ahroun's mother (that's just a bad idea in general because that's how Frenzies happen). While most Garou would not consider such deference to a kin normal, they know better than to risk pissing off a Sept of rage filled warriors by upsetting the boat... because a severe ass-whooping is pretty much the best case scenario. The Shadowlord might think all of that was strange, and perhaps even Litany breaking - but they're never going to say it out loud or act on it and expect a clam rational response.<br /> <br /> For Garou that see kin as family first, an outsider insulting and threatening one of their kin is an attack on the whole family and will be responded to in kind.<br /> <br /> For Garou that see kin more as property first, an outsider and threatening one of their kin is an attack on the host Sept's honor - you don't hit someone else's kin, if you have a problem you take it to the local Alpha/Elder - and a similar result ensues.<br /> <br /> Also, most Garou are raised to some level of meritocracy. If a kin is being honored so thoroughly, the default assumption is that there's a good reason for it; that said kin earned it. There's also always the possibility that the kin in question is also seen as blessed by one of the Totems, Luna, or even Gaia (ex: being a Kami) and there are further reasons you don't see on the surface going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:37:05-08:00","id":1005564,"title":"","content":"Well, the reverence shown in the above scenario stems more from Mama's <i>Sixty Long Years</i> of Humble service, saving the lives of <i>countless</i> mortally-wounded heroes with her Medical and Veterinary expertise, defending/saving the Sept's Children from Black-Spiral Attacks with drawn shotgun, dissolving conflicts by being the mediating voice of calm-reason, giving birth to Garou-Children <i>of her own</i>, and last but *definitely* not least *being there* to Love them as A Mother when they need her.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, being given a warm dinner in your darkest hour and having a Mom's shoulder to cry-on is all that it takes to save you from oblivion. *Sixty* years of endless loyalty, warmth, kindness and love would <i>surely</i> earn some reverence/respect from all but the most ungrateful of Garou septs.<br /> <br /> On a lesser note, I would imagine that even <i>without</i> exemplary service, the average Garou Warrior would STILL calm down from the comforting hug of their Beloved Mother or Father. Even a proud Alpha, no doubt.<br /> <br /> Heck, testosterone-bloated Triad, Gangsta, Yakuza and Mafioso murder-machines in <i>our</i> world are well-documented to be as meek, polite, sweet and gentle as kittens around their mothers.<br /> <br /> Which brings us back to the original subject: A Kinfolk who has successfully raised Metis after Metis to maturity, kept them out of trouble and maybe even raised a notable Hero or Three out of her them would surely be held with *some* (grudging) esteem? Even if this thankless job is often described as a &quot;chore&quot; and &quot;punishment&quot;?<br /> <br /> At the very least, the caretaker in question would more than likely have the respect of &quot;her babies&quot;, if from nobody else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-20-2016, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:59:00-08:00","id":1005573,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you're trying to say.<br /> <br /> Your hypothetical was about an emissary (who wouldn't have had all those experiences with Mama) reacting poorly to the deference given to her by the Garou that do know her. My response was that, especially among the less formal Tribes - the deference thing is reasonable, and that the least plausible aspect was the emissary's faux pas and lack of ability to accept that &quot;honored kin&quot; = &quot;kin that earned respect&quot; and act accordingly.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why there are rules for Kin gaining Renown even if they can't gain Rank like Garou.<br /> <br /> The issue for the original subject is that there's a difference between esteem/respect and formal Rank. Kinfolk can earn all the esteem in the world, but that doesn't grant them formal Rank. Metis can gain formal rank. In the hierarchy of the Garou formal rank &gt; informal esteem as the default, but in individual circumstances it may or may not be held to strictly; and frankly a kinfolk's ability to gain esteem is going to be predicated on them not forcing conflicts of rank and esteem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T21:16:30-08:00","id":1005585,"title":"","content":"Well, my queries more or less stemmed from the passages in &quot;Kinfolk Unsung Heroes&quot; and &quot;Kinfolk A Breed Apart&quot; stating that the words of Kin-Parents as a sad rule fall on deaf ears of their rage-filled children.<br /> <br /> What is more saddening, however, is how it's implied that parents have to <i>defer to their children</i> if they become Garou.<br /> <br /> I always wondered about the truth of those statements.<br /> <br /> As Garou are &quot;only human&quot; (well, 50%), and I doubt that a little rage from the other 50% of your identity is going to change the love and respect you feel for someone who has always been there for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No matter how powerful a warrior you've become, you will always be their Little Boy or Little Girl, and they your Mom or Dad.<br /> <br /> *Surely* the hierarchy system in Garou society does not entitle Garou kids to publicly brush-off their Human parents and disrespect them, right?<br /> <br /> Or is the World of Darkness even darker and crueler than I think it to be? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T21:28:39-08:00","id":1005587,"title":"","content":"I think that it really depends on the viewpoint of the ST. In my games, Kinfolk are equals off of the battlefield, but they are expected to defer to Garou when it comes to combat. Kinfolk take care of everything outside of combat and, for the most part, they make it possible for Garou to fight without worrying about paying the bills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T21:48:35-08:00","id":1005594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1005585#post1005585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As Garou are &quot;only human&quot; (well, 50%), and I doubt that a little rage from the other 50% of your identity is going to change the love and respect you feel for someone who has always been there for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No matter how powerful a warrior you've become, you will always be their Little Boy or Little Girl, and they your Mom or Dad.<br /> *Surely* the hierarchy system in Garou society does not entitle Garou kids to publicly brush-off their Human parents and disrespect them, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I was being asked, but: You can love and respect your parents while still ignoring their words. Kids in our world brush off their parent's advice all the time. Garou can and do do the same. Also, a hug from a mother may or may not be enough to push down Rage. Kinfolk know that and know the risk involved when they intercede. This is not to say that this would fail to calm someone by any means. Just that that is a distinct possibility.<br /> <br /> In the scenario described above, I agree that the emissary should have known better. Even without being familiar with that Sept, you don't hit someone's kin. Pretty much ever. That's idiotic. The Sept though most probably wouldn't have ganged up on him. One (or more) of the Garou present would have stepped up to challenge him immediately. It would have been a formal beating. Not some cowardly dog pile (excusing the pun).<br /> Then the Shadowlord also wouldn't have needed tending to by the Kin. The split is arguably completely unnecessary. But I suppose I'm nitpicking at things that weren't the point of the example. <br /> <br /> So yea, Kin can absolutely be respected among their Sept. And if they've earned Renown (and it sounds like Mama in this scenario has) then she could and should have also been known about before coming to the Sept. An &quot;emissary&quot; would definitely know of her if he were traveling there. <br /> But again, you don't raise your hand to someone's Kin without expecting to come into direct conflict with the Garou (or packs of Garou) in question. I can't see that faux pas happening with someone who was specifically sent to that Sept.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T22:51:14-08:00","id":1005611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1005585#post1005585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my queries more or less stemmed from the passages in &quot;Kinfolk Unsung Heroes&quot; and &quot;Kinfolk A Breed Apart&quot; stating that the words of Kin-Parents as a sad rule fall on deaf ears of their rage-filled children.<br /> <br /> What is more saddening, however, is how it's implied that parents have to <i>defer to their children</i> if they become Garou.<br /> <br /> I always wondered about the truth of those statements...<br /> <br /> ...*Surely* the hierarchy system in Garou society does not entitle Garou kids to publicly brush-off their Human parents and disrespect them, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, remember that the society that both Kinfolk and the Garou inhabit is a highly alien one, and using general human society as a starting point can be very misleading. In Garou society, the Kinfolk are generally viewed as stunted and laughably ignorant <i>at best</i>. Their station in society only goes downhill from there. They have little to no practical experience or knowledge of the spirit world, and lack most of the basic attributes to participate in even the most basic elements of daily Garou life. As such they are generally viewed as little more than &quot;mere&quot; humans. Moreover, the werewolf child generally isn't around after their First Change. That's the point that they basically disappear and spend the rest of their lives getting taught all of &quot;the important things&quot; by other Garou back at the Sept. The Kin just aren't a part of that world. There can be exceptions, but it's not the norm. With few exceptions, the Kin are viewed as supremely inferior by the Garou and their opinions are generally neither sought nor valued.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't think there's a lot of good parallels between this phenomenon in Garou society and in human society. About the best that comes to mind would be a parent that suffers a traumatic brain injury and is reduced to the mental capacity of a four year old. You still love them -- but their opinion just doesn't really matter anymore.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: One other thing: It's not even that the Garou are &quot;disrespecting&quot; the Kin -- <i>exactly</i>. It's that the Kin are expected to &quot;know their place&quot; so to speak, and understand that they're expected to defer to the Garou -- even their own children. It <i>is</i> disrespectful... but only from a human perspective -- not a Garou one. From the Garou perspective, if a Kinfolk fails to defer to their Garou offspring, it's the <i>Kin</i> who is being disrespectful -- by not deferring to his &quot;betters&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-20-2016, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T00:15:52-08:00","id":1005631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1005585#post1005585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my queries more or less stemmed from the passages in &quot;Kinfolk Unsung Heroes&quot; and &quot;Kinfolk A Breed Apart&quot; stating that the words of Kin-Parents as a sad rule fall on deaf ears of their rage-filled children.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a pretty round about way to get to this. Kin don't have Metis children, and while some Kin might be very involved in raising Metis, it's never going to be quite equal to a traditional parent-child relationship (remember that a Metis child is in Crinos for at least 8 years, which is an exceedingly dangerous situation for kin to deal with).<br /> <br /> As others have covered, kin parents with Garou offspring are in a tough situation in terms of dealing with them as parents. You can call it sad, but ultimately it's the nature of things. Imagine what it much be like for non-military parents to have a kid that joins the military at eighteen. They've never been through boot camp. They've never been in a situation with an entirely different concept of appropriate behavior. They've never been deployed to an active combat zone. Without those experience those parents can't say more besides offers of support and love.<br /> <br /> The Garou take this to an extreme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is more saddening, however, is how it's implied that parents have to <i>defer to their children</i> if they become Garou. </div> </div> </div>This is only saddening from specific cultural perspectives. Also, this happens in lesser extents all the time. If your kid becomes town sheriff - or any other position of authority - you're going to have to at least publicly be deferential if you actually care about supporting them. If you speed around town because your kid is the top cop, it's just going to cause trouble.<br /> <br /> In any society where social authority/position is considered more important than familial duty, you're going to see this to some extent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always wondered about the truth of those statements. </div> </div> </div>Like most such statements, they're vague on purpose, and generalizations on purpose.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T04:33:54-08:00","id":1005660,"title":"","content":"have wondered a bit on the Reincarnates, well before they were given that name, ive thought idly ffor years.<br /> <br /> which is a higher step on the totem pole, to them, a silver Fang metis, or a bone gnawer Homid.<br /> <br /> or a metis and a kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T14:06:47-08:00","id":1005846,"title":"","content":"A Metis is evidence of a violation of the litany and a visible stain on the honor of the Silver Fangs. I would think that the majority of such pregnancies would be terminated as soon as they are discoveted, both partners would be punished in a quiet fashion, and honor would be preserved. Anything else would probably be quite unusual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:23:37-08:00","id":1005881,"title":"","content":"The books presentation of things makes is seem like the Garou are fairly anti-abortion (at least among their own). Aborting a Metis is probably done, but most modern Garou are probably taught that if you make a Metis baby, you need to get that Metis to Cliath for Gaia's warriors to have another member (and to make it harder for you to avoid the shame of violating the Litany). The Silver Fangs are definitely treated as liking to deal with Metis pregnancies and births as quietly as possible, but they still end up with Metis in their numbers anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:32:14-08:00","id":1005885,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the very issue Garou have with Metis is also somewhat the reason they tend to get born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:12:41-08:00","id":1005895,"title":"","content":"The problem with Metis, however, is that they incapable of reproducing, which is a much bigger deal in Garou society than American society. Kinfolk can produce more Garou, either by mating with Garou, Kinfolk, or Mortals (Human or Wolf, depending on Breed), while Metis cannot. Metis can be warriors for Gaia, but they will never help to produce more warriors for Gaia, so I imagine that they end up being on point more than Garou who can reproduce. While it may be cold and calculated, better that a Metis get a face full of silver shot than anyone who could reproduce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T17:47:10-08:00","id":1005920,"title":"","content":"Yes. Metis are frequently put in harms way first because of their reduced status among the Garou. But that's got little to do with the pressure to go through with having them over aborting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:15:03-08:00","id":1005990,"title":"","content":"Gonna get this pink elephant out of the room because it will sooner and later run amuck if I don't <br /> <br /> Considering that (1) he can't reproduce (2) Black Furies are as a rule (with few lucky exceptions) a man-hating matriarchy (3) that reveres motherhood and the ability to contribute to motherhood....<br /> <br /> It would be safe to assume that as a rule, a MALE Black Fury Metis would therefore be FAR below the Female Kinfolk of his tribe, and suffer horrific abuse that would make what a Fianna Metis endures seem like &quot;Bambi&quot; in comparison, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-21-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T00:25:51-08:00","id":1006035,"title":"","content":"Not since they retconned in male Metis in the first place, which coincided with severely toning down the &quot;man-hating&quot; thing (after all they still need men to reproduce, so they have to have all those male kinfolk in their Tribe to make that happen).<br /> <br /> A male Metis Black Fury is more pitied than disdained for their sterility, and treating them overly poorly is seen as disrespectful to Pegasus (a masculine spirit who was gelded, so he's got a soft spot for male Metis, and when your Tribal Totem says that male Metis are OK, you listen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T00:35:07-08:00","id":1006039,"title":"","content":"I'd say aborting a metis is a heck of a task that it is not worth it. For one, they regenerate, which means traditional methods are right out. The older books also had this image of fetus metis bursting through their mother's womb like a chestbursters. Unless the mother wants to become infertile, it is just not worth the risks involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T00:54:39-08:00","id":1006045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006039#post1006039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...For one, they regenerate, which means traditional methods are right out...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNot until their First Change, for the most part.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T04:12:26-08:00","id":1006111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006045#post1006045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNot until their First Change, for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is it said that they don't? Yes, homid and lupus don't, but they cannot regen in their breedform anyway. Metis can regen in any form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:21:40-08:00","id":1006361,"title":"","content":"It does not really matter if they regenerate or not during the first trimester. At twelve weeks (or the three weeks for a metis pregnant lupus), a fetus masses half an ounce and is 5 centimeters long, so even a normal human doctor could surgically remove it without any major complications (and would be completely horrified by the level of mutation of the fetus]). Of course, the best solution is to only play with Kinfolk and Mortals (which really should not be that difficult).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:05:07-08:00","id":1006413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006111#post1006111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is it said that they don't? Yes, homid and lupus don't, but they cannot regen in their breedform anyway. Metis can regen in any form.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... your Metis character can't shapeshift -- but he <i>can</i> regenerate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T16:19:59-08:00","id":1006458,"title":"","content":"Is there... something odd about that concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T16:38:59-08:00","id":1006462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006458#post1006458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there... something odd about that concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Before the first change a Metis cannot change into Homid, Lupus, ect, but I don't see why their other stats should be altered. Pre-change Homids cannot regenerate because you can't regenerate in Homid. If a Metis in Crinos can regenerate by default, I see no reason why that is dependent on the First Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T17:43:04-08:00","id":1006482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006462#post1006462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If a Metis in Crinos can regenerate by default, I see no reason why that is dependent on the First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. <br /> I never saw the First Change as a requirement for Metis to regenerate either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T20:29:40-08:00","id":1006543,"title":"","content":".......???<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T20:53:34-08:00","id":1006552,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think I'd rather simplify it to after the first change, Homid form behaves like humans, animal form reacts like the animal for regeneration and soak, allowing the possibility of homids to pass as wolves and lupus to pass as human if they're careful. (Other than certain deformities)<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T21:11:29-08:00","id":1006560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006552#post1006552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think I'd rather simplify it to after the first change, Homid form behaves like humans, animal form reacts like the animal for regeneration and soak, allowing the possibility of homids to pass as wolves and lupus to pass as human if they're careful. (Other than certain deformities)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of the Metamorph merit, Metis can't shapechange before their First Change.<br /> I think the current topic is specifically in regards to Metis and regeneration. If they are stuck in Crinos form, I see no reason why they shouldn't regenerate. They would likewise have a vulnerability to silver from birth, as opposed to after their First Change (which if when I interpret Homids and Lupus' to being taking Agg from Silver).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T23:22:09-08:00","id":1006607,"title":"","content":"Some of the fiction in the books does actually suggest the Metis start minor shapeshifting before their First Change. Nothing useful, just that they naturally start to do little bits of it that they can't really hold for more than a moment. The idea is that the First Change for a Metis is a lot more like a human child going from crawling to riding a bike in that they've been building up to a major milestone that is then used to divide a before/after point, instead of the generally traumatic style First Change of homids and lupus (after all, the Metis' First Change is actually to a weaker form that's in more emotional control).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T03:51:15-08:00","id":1006646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006543#post1006543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.......???</div> </div> </div> </div>What was your take on the subject?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T14:42:00-08:00","id":1006865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006646#post1006646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What was your take on the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>In short: Shapeshifting and regeneration are basically linked traits. (This is actually the first time I've <i>ever</i> encountered someone suggesting otherwise).<br /> <br /> \u200bAs far as the book goes, since Homids and Lupus do not have regeneration prior to their First Change, and<i> do </i>(even in their breed forms) <i>after</i> their First Change, then I would posit that the same is true for Metis. And, <i>yes</i>, Homids do indeed regenerate in Homid form -- and anyone who thinks differently <i>seriously</i> needs to go back and re-read the section on healing on pages 187-188 of W:tA (whichever version was the one that came out in 2000). Humans have a whole chart that covers their recovery times, while Garou (even in breed form) regenerate Lethal at a flat rate of one box per day. Now, for the life of me I can't find it, but I remember somewhere that it got mentioned that this breed-form regeneration is emphatically <i>not</i> available to characters (although admittedly, I don't recall if that explicitly included or excluded Metis) prior to their First Change. (And on a side note, my recollection included an example of pre-Change scars and other injuries remaining with the werewolf for the rest of his life, with regeneration only affecting injuries sustained after the First Change -- if this also rings any bells, somebody please give me a page reference, as it's driving me nuts that I can't find it -- I <i>KNOW</i> I read it somewhere).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T07:25:12-08:00","id":1007228,"title":"","content":"<br /> Well, I'm not sure shapeshifting and regeneration are certainly linked, since Homid and Lupus lack special healing in their normal forms anyway. The language in the revised edition seems to imply some special regeneration ability for Metis. From what I know, a Homid or Lupus can't heal in their natural form, but it notes that Metis specifically can. Being naturally in Crinos gives them the special capability to have increased regeneration in their natural form. But I can't seem to find whether or not that is due to first change either (probably because much of the game is based around playing after change).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T07:59:40-08:00","id":1007246,"title":"","content":"Hm, they heal one health level of lethal per day in their breed form if they are resting (Revised, p. 188). The relevant question is when do Metis undergo First Change and, honestly, I think they experience the First Change in the womb (probably during the second trimester), though they would not learn to consciously change shape until they reach puberty. I do wonder how large a pregnant Garou with a Metis fetus would appear, as a Metis fetus should be around four times as massive as the equivalent human fetus of the same age because they would be in Crinos form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T08:03:54-08:00","id":1007250,"title":"","content":"In W20 the &quot;one level per day&quot; thing only applies when they're resting up after some critical injury, which Metis are noted to not do because they heal at full speed all the time. <br /> <br /> So it might be that homid and lupus garou <i>can</i> heal like that before their first change, but never get a chance to because the trauma that would require it usually triggers the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:39:39-08:00","id":1007320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1005271-metis-social-status-vs-kinfolk-social-status?p=1006865#post1006865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short: Shapeshifting and regeneration are basically linked traits. (This is actually the first time I've <i>ever</i> encountered someone suggesting otherwise).<br /> <br /> \u200bAs far as the book goes, since Homids and Lupus do not have regeneration prior to their First Change, and<i> do </i>(even in their breed forms) <i>after</i> their First Change, then I would posit that the same is true for Metis. And, <i>yes</i>, Homids do indeed regenerate in Homid form -- and anyone who thinks differently <i>seriously</i> needs to go back and re-read the section on healing on pages 187-188 of W:tA (whichever version was the one that came out in 2000). Humans have a whole chart that covers their recovery times, while Garou (even in breed form) regenerate Lethal at a flat rate of one box per day. Now, for the life of me I can't find it, but I remember somewhere that it got mentioned that this breed-form regeneration is emphatically <i>not</i> available to characters (although admittedly, I don't recall if that explicitly included or excluded Metis) prior to their First Change. (And on a side note, my recollection included an example of pre-Change scars and other injuries remaining with the werewolf for the rest of his life, with regeneration only affecting injuries sustained after the First Change -- if this also rings any bells, somebody please give me a page reference, as it's driving me nuts that I can't find it -- I <i>KNOW</i> I read it somewhere).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I've noticed that EVERY aspect of WtA can be up to intrepentation. Cubs rited the same day they Change, garou do not live in a commune, lupus are at the level of feral children mentally and so on.<br /> <br /> But about the metis thing, until we get Changing Ways, Guardians of Caerns is our best source. And it states that little metis children tend to have mini-frenzies, so they all ready have Rage. Granted, I find that rather suspect, not just because it kind of goes against even having a First Change, but also because I cannot imagine a traditional sept ever tolerating a mini-frenzying toddler enough to let it grow to adulthoold. But metis do,unlike homid and lupus, do agg damage in their birth form so in my opinion they are all ready mystically empowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:09:54-08:00","id":1007792,"title":"","content":"Regarding the level of social standing between Metis and Kinfolk I would argue that the situation determines their standing.<br /> <br /> One would dis a metis and basically treat him badly on principle. One would not make fun of or treat the kin daughter of the Warder badly. So, if she is by accident standing in your way, you don't punch her or snarl at her, but politely ask her to step out of your way.<br /> <br /> Different situation however would be any aspect of the garou duties bestowed by Gaia. Garou usually try to keep kin away from this duties, guardian duties at the caern due to low numbers not withstanding. So, a kin who tries to fight that fight might be put in his place, while a metis is given a mission, although usually not those glorious or important...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:52:51-08:00","id":1007815,"title":"","content":"Yes, Kinfolk are to be protected from harm, as they are the future of the Garou, though some Tribes (Get of Fenris) are less protective of their Kinfolk than other Tribes (Children of Gaia). In any case, Garou are in charge when it comes to combat, as Garou are warriors while Kinfolk are support. Metis can be thrown into the meat grinder of combat because they cannot reproduce and, if they die, they will have effectively preserved the life of a Garou who can reproduce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}